it.md`](archive/experiments/2026-10-04_q3_boundary_blocker_audit.md) | 归档审计 | raw MISSING 与异常引用处置前的边界记录 |\\n| [`archive/experiments/2026-10-05_model_sync_blocked.md`](archive/experiments/2026-10-05_model_sync_blocked.md) | 归档诊断 | official Hugging Face path 阻塞记录；已被 mirror success 取代 |\\n## 维护规则\\n\\n1. 顶层、`architecture/`、`datasets/` 和 `governance/` 的现役文件逐项登记。\\n2. `experiments/`、`governance/audit/`、`governance/reference/`、`superpowers/` 按目录登记，不维护逐文件流水账。\\n3. 新文档或归档操作必须与本索引同一提交；归档使用 `git mv`，禁止直接删除。\\n4. 顶层存活文档必须包含“状态 / 更新 / 取代或被取代”头部。\\n5. 当前状态只写 `memory/STATE.md`；未决事项只写 `memory/THREADS.md`；已结案历史保存在 Git、`memory/archive/` 或 `docs/archive/`。\\n6. `HANDOFF.md` 是冻结历史快照，不再作为当前入口。\\n## 导师讨论包（2026-10-09）\\n\\n| 文件 | 状态 | 用途 |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| [`../paper/advisor_discussion_brief_2026-10-09.md`](../paper/advisor_discussion_brief_2026-10-09.md) | 内部讨论草稿 | 30 秒研究故事、Stage E 证据、evidence ceiling 与两项导师决策 |\\n| [`../paper/advisor_decision_tables_2026-10-09.md`](../paper/advisor_decision_tables_2026-10-09.md) | `RECOMMENDATION_ONLY` | multi-leaf vs second dataflow、harmfulness 三种定义决策表 |\\n| [`archive/current_status_reconciliation_proposal.md`](archive/current_status_reconciliation_proposal.md) | `PROPOSAL_ONLY` | stale statement 标记与 README/STATE patch proposal；尚未应用 |\\n| [`archive/2026-10-09_advisor_decision_candidate_paths.md`](archive/2026-10-09_advisor_decision_candidate_paths.md) | `AWAITING_ADVISOR_DECISION` | Path M / Path D 候选执行计划；禁止自动执行 |\\n\\n## Stage E 方法修正与 Stage D 参考轨（2026-10-09）\\nDeliverables: [metric priority](research/stage_e_metric_priority_v2.md), [HBR boundary](research/stage_e_harmfulness_metric_boundary_v1.md), [zero-event uncertainty](research/stage_e_zero_event_uncertainty_note_v1.md), [matched-FPR protocol](research/stage_e_matched_fpr_reanalysis_protocol_v1.md), [matched-FPR reanalysis](research/stage_e_matched_fpr_reanalysis_v1.md), [NIST ledger](research/nist_measurement_validity_ledger_v2.md), [multi-leaf preregistration](research/stage_e_multileaf_preregistration_v1.md), [power plan](research/stage_e_multileaf_power_plan_v1.md), [PRM800K audit](research/prm800k_reference_track_audit_v1.md), [Math-Shepherd audit](research/math_shepherd_reference_track_audit_v1.md), [process-signal requirements](research/stage_d_process_signal_requirements_v1.md), [paper upgrade plan](research/stage_e_paper_upgrade_plan_v1.md).\\nSupporting validation: [`../research/stage_e_method_revision_20261009/stage_e_method_revision_receipt.json`](../research/stage_e_method_revision_20261009/stage_e_method_revision_receipt.json). Current indexed additions: [FORMAL_EXPERIMENT_PREFLIGHT_V1.md](governance/FORMAL_EXPERIMENT_PREFLIGHT_V1.md), [GRAPH_LOOP_AUTHORITY_MAP_V1.md](governance/GRAPH_LOOP_AUTHORITY_MAP_V1.md), [overnight_graph_loop_handoff_2026-10-10.md](archive/overnight_graph_loop_handoff_2026-10-10.md), [repository_governance_audit_loop_c_contract.md](handoff/repository_governance_audit_loop_c_contract.md), [repository_governance_inventory_loop_a_contract.md](handoff/repository_governance_inventory_loop_a_contract.md), [repository_governance_local_truth_addendum_2026-10-11.md](handoff/repository_governance_local_truth_addendum_2026-10-11.md), [2026-10-08_stage_e_inquiry_and_experiment_design_v1.md](research/2026-10-08_stage_e_inquiry_and_experiment_design_v1.md), [agent_distillation_adapter_provenance_audit_v1.md](research/agent_distillation_adapter_provenance_audit_v1.md), [agent_distillation_tcv_execution_smoke_v1.md](research/agent_distillation_tcv_execution_smoke_v1.md), [derived_process_supervision_design_v1.md](research/derived_process_supervision_design_v1.md), [finqa_causal_exposure_preregistration_proposal_v1.md](research/finqa_causal_exposure_preregistration_proposal_v1.md), [finqa_numeric_token_canonicalization_v2.md](research/finqa_numeric_token_canonicalization_v2.md), [finqa_process_checkpoint_v2_preregistration_draft_v1.md](research/finqa_process_checkpoint_v2_preregistration_draft_v1.md), [finqa_v2_candidate_sample_manifest_v1.md](research/finqa_v2_candidate_sample_manifest_v1.md), [finqa_v2_causal_join_audit_v1.md](research/finqa_v2_causal_join_audit_v1.md), [finqa_v2_gate_reconciliation_v2.md](research/finqa_v2_gate_reconciliation_v2.md), [finqa_v2_gate_status_v1.md](research/finqa_v2_gate_status_v1.md), [finqa_v2_overlap_feasibility_v1.md](research/finqa_v2_overlap_feasibility_v1.md), [itil_ai_governance_background_evidence_v1.md](research/itil_ai_governance_background_evidence_v1.md), [math_shepherd_label_quality_sensitivity_v1.md](research/math_shepherd_label_quality_sensitivity_v1.md), [math_shepherd_label_smoke_v1.md](research/math_shepherd_label_smoke_v1.md), [multileaf_mechanism_generalization_audit_v1.md](research/multileaf_mechanism_generalization_audit_v1.md), [multileaf_preresult_freeze_receipt_v1.md](research/multileaf_preresult_freeze_receipt_v1.md), [nist_tevv_background_evidence_v1.md](research/nist_tevv_background_evidence_v1.md), [prm_c2_c4_selection_dryrun_v1.md](research/prm_c2_c4_selection_dryrun_v1.md), [prm_reference_training_smoke_audit_addendum_v1.md](research/prm_reference_training_smoke_audit_addendum_v1.md), [prm_reference_training_smoke_v1.md](research/prm_reference_training_smoke_v1.md), [process_supervision_adaptation_review_v1.md](research/process_supervision_adaptation_review_v1.md), [stage_d_minimal_experiment_v2.md](research/stage_d_minimal_experiment_v2.md), [stage_d_prm_formal_pilot_proposal_v1.md](research/stage_d_prm_formal_pilot_proposal_v1.md), [stage_e_118_quantification_v1.md](research/stage_e_118_quantification_v1.md), [stage_e_independent_scorer_feasibility_v1.md](research/stage_e_independent_scorer_feasibility_v1.md), [stage_e_metric_precedent_review_v1.md](research/stage_e_metric_precedent_review_v1.md), [stage_e_multileaf_protocol_v2.md](research/stage_e_multileaf_protocol_v2.md), [stage_e_multileaf_result_packet_v1.md](research/stage_e_multileaf_result_packet_v1.md), [stage_e_multileaf_signature_ablation_v1.md](research/stage_e_multileaf_signature_ablation_v1.md), [stage_e_multileaf_v2_robustness_preregistration_delta_v1.md](research/stage_e_multileaf_v2_robustness_preregistration_delta_v1.md), [stage_e_narrative_after_advisor_feedback_v1.md](research/stage_e_narrative_after_advisor_feedback_v1.md), [stage_e_observability_metrics_v1.md](research/stage_e_observability_metrics_v1.md), [stage_e_second_dataflow_candidate_qualification_v1.md](research/stage_e_second_dataflow_candidate_qualification_v1.md), [stage_e_stage_d_unified_story_v1.md](research/stage_e_stage_d_unified_story_v1.md), [stage_e_threshold_visibility_analysis_v1.md](research/stage_e_threshold_visibility_analysis_v1.md), [stage_e_version_b_figure_spec_v1.md](research/stage_e_version_b_figure_spec_v1.md), [stage_e_version_b_revision_proposal_v1.md](research/stage_e_version_b_revision_proposal_v1.md).\\n## Independent C Audits (2026-10-10)\\n\\n[multi-leaf](experiments/2026-10-10_loop_c_multileaf_audit.md), [PRM smoke](experiments/2026-10-10_loop_c_prm_smoke_audit.md), [binding-v2](experiments/2026-10-10_loop_c_finqa_v2_binding_v2_audit.md), and [Graph Loop governance](experiments/2026-10-10_loop_c_graph_loop_meta_retrospective_audit.md).\\n\\n## SANER Route Lock and Repository Governance (2026-10-11)\\n\\nRoute A scope: [scope lock](../paper/saner_rene_manuscript_scope_lock_v1.md) and [claim matrix](../paper/saner_rene_claim_matrix_v1.json). Route B is [NO / STOP_BRANCH](research/route_b_read_only_qualification_2026-10-11.md). FinQA interpretation is recorded in [measurement-object autopsy](research/finqa_v2_measurement_object_mismatch_autopsy_v1.md). Governance inventory, lineage and [commit manifest](handoff/repository_governance_commit_manifest_2026-10-11.json) are in [handoff](handoff/repository_governance_and_sync_2026-10-11.md) and [FinQA lineage](research/finqa_v2_asset_lineage_v1.md) and [final C audit](experiments/2026-10-11_loop_c_repository_governance_final_audit.md) and [cross-host PASS receipt](experiments/2026-10-11_cross_host_receipt_verification.json).\\nFormal-v3 authorization/task-ID reconciliation is recorded in [activation record](research/finqa_v2_formal_v3_activation_record_v1.md).\\n# SKILL_ROUTING.md — skill 路由法（治理线立法, 2026-08-29）\\n\\n> 状态: 活跃（立法件, 修改需用户批） | 更新: 2026-10-08 | 取代/被取代: 无 | 依据: 侧线设计稿转述（用户卡 08-29）+ 注册表↔分发漂移事故（30 件, 08-29 修复）+ skill 库扩容精简化（09-18 批 #6-S: 49 件新 skill 入库、12 件旧件删除）+ **skill 语义合并（09-21 批 #8-A: 10 簇合并, 目录 108→92; 五线主装按合并后名重列, §3 裁定表逐字保留不回改）**\\n> 范围: 六线任务的 skill 装载决策; 与根 AGENTS.md 配属注册表互为表里（注册表 = 有什么, 本法 = 何时用）\\n\\n## 1 六线总表（任务线 → 主装 skill）\\n\\n| 线 | 主装（按需, 单任务 ≤5） | 常备背景（不占配额） |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 论文线 | research-writing-skill / algorithm-description / paper-review-check / paper-polish-and-audit / scientific-toolkit-skill | graph-loop-rules |\\n| 治理线 | neat-freak / jinrong-docs-sync / code-cleanup-helper / skill-doctor / skill-map / repo-audit / readme-audit | graph-loop-rules |\\n| 运维线 | systematic-debugging / m1-gap-triage / m2-rag-playbook / graph-loop-rules / experiment-autopsy / shift-notes / experiment-analysis / train-monitor / gpu-env | graph-loop-rules |\\n| 前端线 | playwright / frontend-quality / verify-before-done | graph-loop-rules |\\n| 工程线 | testing-practices / git-history-ops / code-simplification / commit-and-pr-hygiene / db-schema-change / systematic-debugging / secret-scan / input-validation / dependency-audit / eval-harness / progress-reading-protocol | graph-loop-rules |\\n| 交付线 | office-academic-skill / pdf / verify-before-done | graph-loop-rules |\\n| 调研/决策线 | inquiry-methods / socrates / paper-review-check / research-driven-design / decision-record | graph-loop-rules |\\n\\n## 2 仲裁规则（冲突时依次适用）\\n\\n1. **红线永载**: 涉及冻结节点/生产后端/甲方数据/对外发送的任务, `graph-loop-rules` 无条件装载, 不占配额。\\n2. **领域优先**: 任务领域词命中某线 → 该线主装优先于通用件（如\\\"论文草稿\\\"→ 论文线, 不装通用 review-codebase）。\\n3. **单任务 ≤5**: 装载清单超过 5 件 = 过装备（认知负载 > 收益, 见 tool-restraint 主张）; 超出者移入\\\"可选\\\"注记不装载。\\n4. **新旧降级**: 同职能新旧两件并存时, 新版装载、旧版标 DEPRECATED 不删（治理规则 4 先例）; 引用旧版的历史工件不改。\\n5. **显式优于推断**: 卡片装载清单 > 触发词推断; 推断装载必须在开工注记里写明理由。\\n\\n## 3 冗余裁决表（点名裁定, 2026-08-29）\\n\\n| 件 | 裁定 | 理由 |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| verification-before-completion | **已废（DEPRECATED 标记）** | 已并入 verify-before-done（对抗式审查 + 完成门两段式, 2026-07-28 合并）; 新任务一律装后者 |\\n| paper-review-check vs paper-polish-and-audit | **分工并存**: 过程审查用前者, 投稿终审用后者 | review-check = 草稿期逻辑/一致性/审稿风险（每章过一遍）; polish-audit = 定稿期术语锁定/主张核验/编译检查（投稿前一次） |\\n| pdf 双份（仓库版 + 个人版） | **合一: 仓库版为准** | 仓库 skills/ = source of truth（三层分发架构）; 个人版仅作未同步兜底, 不得反向回灌覆盖 |\\n| figma × 6 / cloudflare-deploy / vercel-deploy | **标个人通用, 不主动装载** | 本项目无 Figma/部署工作流; 仅用户显式要求时装载; 注册表保留（分发实况对齐）但路由表不列 |\\n| recsys-toolkit | 个人职业工具, 不入项目路由 | 触发词 /recsys, 与五线无关 |\\n| vibe-coding × 6（context-manager / planner / principles / prompt-engineer / quality-gate / refinement） | **已删（09-18 批 #6-S, 用户裁定）** | 旧世代自洽管线, 职责已被 spec-first + sprint-contract + executing-plans 覆盖; 互引随删消失 |\\n| code-review / generate-commit / memory-systems / multi-agent-patterns / tool-design / webapp-testing | **已删（09-18 批 #6-S, 用户裁定）** | 与 C 侧现役件职责重叠; 删前实测前 5 件零入向引用, code-review 仅被 code-pathology 的 tags 引用 |\\n| subagent-fanout vs dispatching-parallel-agents vs subagent-driven-development | **分工并存**: 通用概览 / 计划内多步执行 / 新件=精确并行 fanout | 三者粒度不同, 暂不合并（skill-merger 可后续评估） |\\n| owasp-review / sql-review / authz-check / input-validation / secret-scan | **分工并存（新件, 09-18 入库）** | 分别覆盖安全 diff 审查 / SQL 正确性 / 授权越权 / 边界输入 / 密钥扫描, 互不替代 |\\n| 09-21 批 #8-A 的 10 簇合并 | **10 簇合并已执行（用户 09-21 裁定）** | C1 research-writing-skill(合 paper-writing-zh) / C2 experiment-analysis(合 experiment-observer) / C3 commit-and-pr-hygiene(3) / C4 code-simplification(3) / C5 git-history-ops(3) / C6 db-schema-change(2) / C7 frontend-quality(3) / C8 testing-practices(4) / C12 progress-reading-protocol(合 broken-window-check) / C13 eval-harness(合 evaluator-calibration); 目录 108→92, A 93→77, C 21→21 |\\n| 09-21 批 #8-A 的四个「保持现状」 | **不合并（用户 09-21 裁定）** | C9 web-deploy 延后 / C10 codebase-review 延后 / C11 paper-audit 保持分工并存（§3 原裁定有效） / C15 dispatching-parallel-agents 保持不合并（§3 原裁定有效） |\\n| verification-before-completion 摘除 | **已执行（09-21 批 #9-B, 三步同一 commit）** | C14+A19 落地: (i) `docs_lint [5]` 跳过用途列含 DEPRECATED 的注册表行 + 输出一条 INFO 行; (ii) 从 `A_SKILLS` 摘除该件（A 77→76, 总数 98→97）; (iii) prune 安装区残留（实测仅 `~/.codex/skills` 一端有副本）。注册表行按治理规则 4 保留 |\\n\\n## 4 钩链矩阵（机械强制层 × 自动装载）\\n\\n| 钩/环 | 自动关联 | 说明 |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| pre-commit index-guard | jinrong-docs-sync（事后） | 新文档未登记被拦 → 收口时装载补登记 |\\n| pre-commit large-file-guard | 无 skill | 纯机械 |\\n| Loop B 验证 | 无（纯 bash） | 不装 AI |\\n| Loop C 审计派单 | differential-review / paper-review-check（论文件, 08-29 扩围） | 审计对象决定 |\\n| 收口清单漂移扫描 | neat-freak（命中多时装载清场） | governance_drift_scan 命中 ≥10 触发 |\\n| 实验窗开/收 | sprint-contract + verify-before-done | 窗口卡标配两件 |\\n\\n## 5 装载纪律（卡片义务）\\n\\n1. 任务卡必须含\\\"**skill 装载清单**\\\"行: 列出本任务实际装载件（≤5 + 红线常备）, 空 = 声明\\\"无需装载\\\"。\\n2. 推断装载需一句话理由; 显式装载照录卡文。\\n3. 收口汇报附装载清单执行情况（装了没用 / 没用装 = 浪费信号, 记台账供路由表迭代）。\\n4. 路由表每季度（或漂移事故后）复审一次, 修订需用户批（立法件纪律）。\\n| formal experiment preflight | verify-before-done + audit-cycle + self-eval-bias | `FORMAL_EXPERIMENT_PREFLIGHT_V1.md`; END_TO_END_PREFLIGHT_PASS 前禁止 scientific output |\\n| authority/handoff closure | neat-freak + jinrong-docs-sync | `GRAPH_LOOP_AUTHORITY_MAP_V1.md`; A/C/D handoff 必须带 authority paths + hashes + PASS level |\\n---\\nname: graph-loop-rules\\ndescription: JinRongAgents Graph Loop 红线与运行约束。OpenCode agent 在本仓库执行任何任务（解析、审计、问答、代码修改）前必须遵守；涉及冻结节点、生产后端、API key、72B 模型时触发。\\n---\\n\\n# Graph Loop 运行约束（OpenCode agent 适用）\\n\\n本仓库运行四层 Graph Loop（A 执行 / B 验证 / C 审计 / D 战略，见 docs/17）。任何 agent 任务必须遵守：\\n\\n## 红线（违反即失败）\\n1. 冻结节点不可修改：tests/test_m1_service.py、scripts/graph/frozen_hashes.txt、docs/m1_schema/（schema 基线文档）、以及 frozen_hashes.txt 所列全部路径（含仓库外运行时 schema ~/wzh/m1_samples/m1_table_schema.json，commit 钩子 + Loop B 双重 md5 校验）。注意：仓库内 config/m1_table_schema.json 不在冻结清单，可通过 schema API 写入并热加载（见 m1-gap-triage skill）。\\n2. 不改不重启 :5050 生产后端（甲方演示随时可用）；不切页面后端。\\n3. 不触碰、不打印、不创建 API key。\\n4. 不加载 72B 模型（已终判退化并删除）。\\n5. 归档文档用 git mv，禁止 rm；OpenCode/MCP 交付物三件（archive/09、archive/10、archive/2026-07-19_m2_mcp_verification.md）永不删除。\\n\\n## 运行纪律\\n- 每步任务结果追加到 logs/graph/dispatch_log.md（格式：[HH:MM] 任务 → 结果 → commit）。\\n- 无法判断的问题写 logs/graph/blocked_questions.md 后跳过，不阻塞。\\n- gap/遗留项台账唯一信源：memory/THREADS.md，其他文档只引用不复述。\\n- 现状以 memory/STATE.md 为准，不到历史文档里找现状。\\n- Loop A 执行层完整约束见 scripts/graph/loop_a_exec_constraints.md；Loop C 审计 prompt 见 scripts/graph/loop_c_audit_prompt.md。\\n- 需要联网检索或数值验证时用 python scripts/qwen_harness_tools.py（web_search / code_interpreter / web_extractor），不滥用。\\n\\n## 验证要求\\n交付前必须：远端 ./venv/bin/python -m pytest -q 全绿（基线 275 passed / 13 skipped）；证据先于断言（evidence before assertions）。\\n--- card ---\\n# Loop A Assignment - TAT-QA WP-1 (thin runner: checker + adapter + fixtures + preflight; NO MODEL CALLS)\\n\\nCARD: research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/loop_a_prompt.md | dispatched 2026-10-13 by Loop D under owner approval.\\nROLE: Loop A / GB10 implementation. You implement ONE bounded software package (WP-1) plus its non-scientific fixture checks. Nothing else. Model calls = 0. This card authorises NO pilot run and NO episode collection.\\n\\nCONTRACT (read first; binding):\\n- docs/research/WP0_TATQA_ADAPTER_CHECKER_CONTRACT_v1.md  (THE specification for checker/adapter/fixtures)\\n- docs/research/WP0_TATQA_LOOP_A_EXECUTION_PACKAGE_v1.md  (W1-W5 + acceptance criteria)\\n- docs/research/WP0_TATQA_EVALUATION_PROTOCOL_v1.md  (context only; do not execute anything)\\n- data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/origin_manifest.json, candidate_items_v1.json, GENERATION_RECEIPT.json  (READ-ONLY)\\n- data/research/tatqa_raw_2026/tatqa_dataset_train.json, tatqa_dataset_dev.json  (READ-ONLY)\\n\\nProject dir (your cwd): /home/testuser/wzh/projects/agents_final_tech\\nWork dir (create; NEW): research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/\\nData out (create; NEW): data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/\\n\\nPINNED INPUTS (verify BEFORE anything else; mismatch -> STOP, report HASH_MISMATCH):\\n- candidate_items_v1.json sha256 bc55fe7a53381f32e5d84ff6c17ced18ec72fd322f98a9f80c4eccb714caac12\\n- origin_manifest.json sha256 3718e6fef4d52bec0c1c29b47ba9ab60e298754b9e8527835d09c9d223d70cea\\n- tatqa_dataset_train.json sha256 2df6e722cdbaaa37efcbfb280f5c9a15be29a6ec18f618ef936fe63cc6d07c69\\n- tatqa_dataset_dev.json sha256 8da095a819af6db3c14877c6df2d4d29960e41d1a63dd1fa853507bd2a616af5\\n- expected counts: 60 candidate items; 182 origins.\\n\\nPRE-RUN (mandatory order):\\n1) Verify the four hashes (sha256sum) and the two counts from GENERATION_RECEIPT.json.\\n2) Write research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/implementation_contract.md first: module list, function signatures, fixture plan, receipt schema, exact commands you will run; hash the contract before running anything.\\n3) Implement W1-W5, then run ONLY the synthetic fixture suite.\\n\\nWORK ITEMS (spec = adapter/checker contract; acceptance = execution package Sec.2):\\nW1 checker.py - gold recomputed from table cells (strip thousands separators; parentheses = negative), scale conversion (thousand->unit, million->thousand, billion->million, percent->percent), outcome taxonomy including correct_other_form / REFUSED / UNKNOWN; gold exists before any answer is read.\\nW2 adapter.py - deterministic actor-visible projection (verbatim, no truncation), fixed answer format, hidden fields (gold etc.) never leaked, opaque item/origin ids, byte-identical prompt for the same item+arm; arm context hooks for B/E/C/S as typed placeholders only (real experience blocks are NOT built here).\\nW3 fixtures/ + run_fixtures.py - the six obligations: (1) byte-equal prompts; (2) hidden-gold string search clean; (3) >=5 hand-built recompute fixtures incl. one parentheses-negative and one thousands-separator case; (4) the four scale conversions; (5) UNKNOWN + REFUSED classification; (6) E/C context token-delta accounting. SYNTHETIC fixtures only; never read held-out outcomes.\\nW4 PREFLIGHT_RECEIPT.json - required files exist; schema field names match the runtime payload; checker defined on all allowed inputs; group/split ids resolve; provenance writer attributes to this task; the metric pipeline runs end-to-end on NON-SCIENTIFIC fixtures; no held-out result read.\\nW5 PREREG_DRAFT_SKELETON.md + hash pins (checker/adapter/fixtures/preflight hashes); actor fields marked PENDING (advisor selection; do NOT touch model files or weights).\\n\\nSTYLE: python3 stdlib only; LF outputs; tests runnable via `python3 research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/run_fixtures.py`; no pytest dependency.\\n\\nFORBIDDEN: model/judge calls; network; services/databases; training; commit/push; editing paper/, docs/, pinned inputs, or anything outside the two write dirs; scoring candidate items (READ allowed, SCORE not allowed; fixtures are synthetic); running loop_b_verify.sh; fabricating or weakening any test.\\nSTOP CONDITIONS: hash mismatch -> HASH_MISMATCH; any fixture obligation fails -> STOP and report SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED naming the failing item (never adjust the test to pass); a forbidden action being required -> stop and report.\\n\\nOUTPUTS: the files above + research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/WP1_RECEIPT.json (valid JSON, no fences): task, start/end UTC, re-verified input hashes, artifact hashes (checker/adapter/fixtures/preflight/contract), per-obligation fixture results, preflight results, cost (model_calls=0, endpoint_calls=0), unverified items, deviations (expect none).\\n\\nEND: final message = status + receipt path + one-line summary.\\n--- checker contract ---\\n# WP-0 TAT-QA Adapter and Checker Contracts v1\\n\\n> date: 2026-10-13 | author: Loop D (WP-0 item A5) | status: `SPECIFICATION_ONLY - NOT IMPLEMENTED`\\n> parents: [WP0_TATQA_PACKAGE_v1.md](WP0_TATQA_PACKAGE_v1.md), [task card](thesis_experience_v1_task_card.md), [blueprint](THESIS_EXECUTION_BLUEPRINT_v1.md) §2\\n> These contracts describe what Loop A must implement in WP-1. Nothing here is code, and nothing here authorises a run.\\n\\n## 1. Task adapter contract\\n\\n**Input:** one candidate item from `data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/candidate_items_v1.json`.\\n\\n**Actor-visible projection (what the model sees):**\\n- the table (all rows and columns, verbatim, no truncation per arm);\\n- the two period labels and the row label/identifier needed to name the row;\\n- the requested quantity and the requested target unit;\\n- the tool description (a deterministic calculator: `calc(expression) -> number`);\\n- the arm-specific context block (none for B; the experience block for E/C; the static rules for S).\\n\\n**Hidden from the actor, always:** `gold_delta_source_unit`, `gold_recompute_rule`, any derived target value, the item's origin id where it would leak the answer, and the whole `candidate_items` file.\\n\\n**Actor obligations:** choose the row, the two periods, the unit relation and the arithmetic parameter; call the calculator; the final answer must consume the calculator's returned value.\\n\\n**Answer format (fixed):** `{row: <label>, periods: [<late>, <early>], delta_source: <number>, delta_target: <number>, unit: <target unit>}` in a single JSON object, or the literal token `REFUSED` / `UNKNOWN`.\\n\\n**Determinism:** the adapter must produce byte-identical prompts for the same item and arm. No timestamps, no sampling, no arm-dependent table truncation.\\n\\n## 2. Checker contract\\n\\n**Gold recomputation (independent of the actor):** for the item's `row_index`, read `value(late)` and `value(early)` from the table cells with the stated parser (strip thousands separators, treat parentheses as negative), compute `delta_source = value(late) - value(early)`, then convert by the scale factor between `source_unit` and the requested target unit. The checker must never read the actor's output before the gold exists.\\n\\n**Scoring (per item, per arm, per repeat):**\\n| Outcome | Rule |\\n|---|---|\\n| `correct` | `delta_source` and `delta_target` both match gold exactly (after the declared rounding); row and periods match |\\n| `correct_other_form` | same value via a mathematically equivalent expression (e.g., early-minus-late with a negated sign) - counted as correct, and recorded separately |\\n| `wrong_unit` | `delta_source` correct but `delta_target` wrong |\\n| `wrong_period` | the periods chosen differ from the item's |\\n| `regressed` | compared to arm B on the same item, a previously correct answer becomes incorrect |\\n| `refused` | the literal `REFUSED` |\\n| `unknown` | the literal `UNKNOWN`, a timeout, or an unparseable answer |\\n\\n**Independent unit of analysis:** the origin (the raw record), not the item, not the repeat. Report per-origin paired differences `E-B`, `E-C`, `E-S`, `C-B`, with the origin-level differences listed explicitly.\\n\\n**Anti-leakage obligations the checker must enforce:** (a) the item's gold appears nowhere in the actor-visible projection; (b) no item shares an origin with any experience episode used in the same arm run; (c) the C-arm context differs from the E-arm context by at most 5% in context tokens; (d) the S-arm rules are frozen at development time and never edited per item.\\n\\n## 3. Fixture obligations (what Loop A must demonstrate without any model)\\n\\nOn synthetic fixtures only, Loop A must show:\\n1. the adapter emits the same prompt twice for the same item (byte equality);\\n2. the gold never appears in the projection (string search);\\n3. the checker's recomputation matches hand-computed values on at least 5 hand-built fixtures, including one with parentheses-negative cells and one with a thousands separator;\\n4. the scale conversion matches for thousand->unit, million->thousand, billion->million and percent->percent;\\n5. an `UNKNOWN` and a `REFUSED` answer are classified correctly;\\n6. the arm-context token delta between E and C is computed and reported.\\n\\n**Stop:** if any fixture obligation cannot be met, WP-1 stops and reports `SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED`. No model is called to \\\"try it out\\\".--- execution package ---\\n# WP-0 TAT-QA Loop A Execution Package v1 (DRAFT - NOT DISPATCHED)\\n\\n> date: 2026-10-13 | author: Loop D | status: `READY_TO_DISPATCH_AFTER_APPROVAL` | zero model calls; fixture-first; no training.\\n> parents: [adapter/checker contract](WP0_TATQA_ADAPTER_CHECKER_CONTRACT_v1.md), [evaluation protocol](WP0_TATQA_EVALUATION_PROTOCOL_v1.md), [task card](thesis_experience_v1_task_card.md) Sec.3-4, [exec constraints](../../scripts/graph/loop_a_exec_constraints.md), [launcher](../governance/loop_ac_launcher_v1.md).\\n\\n## 1. Preconditions (all required before dispatch)\\n\\n1. Advisor: G-RQ accepted (QUALIFIED_CONDITIONAL -> formal allowance for WP-1).\\n2. Owner/advisor: write-path permission for `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/` and `data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/` on GB10.\\n3. Actor freeze plan approved for the later stages (F1); WP-1 itself needs no model.\\n4. Dispatch via `scripts/graph/loop_ac_launcher.sh` (the designed channel), prompt file in-repo, receipt discipline per the launcher doc.\\n\\n## 2. Work items (all reversible; fixture-first; stdlib-only where possible)\\n\\n| # | Item | Deliverable | Acceptance |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| W1 | Checker implementation | `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/checker.py` (+ tests) | matches hand-computed values on 5 fixtures incl. parentheses-negative and thousands separator; taxonomy classes incl. `REFUSED`/`UNKNOWN` |\\n| W2 | Adapter implementation | `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/adapter.py` (+ tests) | byte-identical prompts for same item+arm; hidden-gold search clean; opaque ids; no arm-dependent truncation |\\n| W3 | Fixture suite (A5 Sec.3, six obligations) | `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/fixtures/` + receipt | all six obligations PASS, incl. E/C token-delta computation; fail-closed |\\n| W4 | Execution preflight | `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/PREFLIGHT_RECEIPT.json` | required files exist; schema fields match runtime payload; scorer defined on allowed inputs; provenance writer attributes to the task; metric pipeline runs on NON-SCIENTIFIC fixtures; no held-out reads |\\n| W5 | Freeze assembly (with Loop D) | prereg draft + hash pins | protocol/item/split/actor/checker hashes resolve |\\n\\n## 3. Non-goals / prohibitions\\n\\n- No model calls, no episode collection, no context-block construction, no training (Memory/SFT/DPO), no production services, no change to any frozen Paper E asset.\\n- No edits outside the two write paths above; receipts required for every claim; `SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED` stop on any fixture failure (do not \\\"try it out\\\" with a model).\\n\\n## 4. Stop and escalation\\n\\n- Any acceptance failure -> stop, report `SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED` with the failing fixture.\\n- After W1-W5 PASS + C pre-result audit PASS -> only then request pilot (WP-2) authorisation; budget/window must be bound first.\\n\\n## 5. Dispatch template (when approved)\\n\\n```\\nbash scripts/graph/loop_ac_launcher.sh start a tatqa-wp1-<date> research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/loop_a_prompt.md 14400\\n```\\n\\nPrompt file must state: scope = W1-W5 only; write paths; receipts; fail-closed; no model/services.\\n--- evaluation protocol ---\\n# WP-0 TAT-QA Evaluation Protocol v1 (SPEC)\\n\\n> date: 2026-10-13 | author: Loop D | status: `SPEC_ONLY - NOT EXECUTABLE` | no experiment, no model call, no training.\\n> parents: [task card](thesis_experience_v1_task_card.md) Sec.2-4, [blueprint](THESIS_EXECUTION_BLUEPRINT_v1.md) Sec.2, [package](WP0_TATQA_PACKAGE_v1.md) Sec.5, [adapter/checker contract](WP0_TATQA_ADAPTER_CHECKER_CONTRACT_v1.md). Numbers below are inherited, not new.\\n\\n## 1. Question and scope\\n\\nIn a fixed actor / tool / budget setting, does providing related real execution experience from other origins improve answer correctness (including unit and period) and matched execution behaviour on new-origin two-period table-calculation tasks? This protocol covers the minimal validation (WP-2) only; it does not test feedback-construction algorithms, memory updating, parameter learning, or adaptation claims.\\n\\n## 2. Population and units\\n\\n- Item pool: the frozen candidate list (60 items / 60 distinct origins; `data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/candidate_items_v1.json`; gold recomputed by the checker from cells).\\n- Independent unit of analysis: the **origin** (raw record). Not the item, not the repeat.\\n- Splits (sizes inherited from the card/blueprint): history = 8 episodes from >= 4 origins; development = 4 tasks from >= 2 origins; pilot = 16 tasks from **8 unseen origins** (2 tasks per origin), each run twice.\\n- Isolation: test origins share no origin with history/development; near-duplicate isolation across arms; test gold never enters any context.\\n\\n## 3. Arms (frozen definitions)\\n\\n| Arm | Context | What it isolates |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| B | none | base capability and headroom |\\n| E | 1-2 related real executed episodes (other origins) | effect of the experience package vs B |\\n| C | matched unrelated experience, same format; E/C context token delta <= 5% | whether the *relatedness* matters |\\n| S | static unit/period rules frozen at development | whether a cheap non-experience rule already explains gains |\\n\\nAll arms receive the same complete task evidence; no arm-dependent table truncation. One actor revision (see freeze plan), two model calls per episode (plan -> tool execution -> consume result), reset between items, no memory write-back.\\n\\n## 4. Calls and budget (inherited; hard)\\n\\n4 arms x 16 tasks x 2 repeats = 128 episodes; <= 256 evaluation requests; history+development <= 40; transport retries <= 4; **hard cap 300 actor request attempts, 0 judge calls**. Input/output caps and the 600-token experience block per the card Sec.3.4.\\n\\n## 5. Endpoints and reporting\\n\\n- Primary: per-item outcome class from the checker taxonomy (`correct`, `correct_other_form`, `wrong_unit`, `wrong_period`, `regressed`, `refused`, `unknown`).\\n- Effects: per-origin paired differences `E-B`, `E-C`, `E-S`, `C-B`; list every origin-level difference explicitly; count corrections, regressions, refusals, UNKNOWN; report token/cost accounting per arm.\\n- Uncertainty: origin-level bootstrap CI (method declared in the prereg); no new significance thresholds; UNKNOWN stays a first-class state.\\n- Honesty rules: no pooled success showcase; behaviour change is reported but never asserted as causal by itself; window/scale of the pilot explicitly not extrapolated.\\n\\n## 6. Gates and stop rules (inherited; unchanged)\\n\\n| Outcome | Ruling |\\n|---|---|\\n| `E-B` and `E-C` each >= +12.5pp, >= 3 net-positive origins, no origin > 50% of its arm's corrections, both repeats non-reversing, behaviour consistent | `CONTINUE_EXPLORATORY` (apply for baseline/necessity comparison only) |\\n| B perfect on both repeats; leakage or bridge failure; B ceiling | `STOP_THIS_PANEL` / invalid per cause; do not add difficulty to hunt an effect |\\n| S solves everything | `NEW_METHOD_NOT_NECESSARY_ON_THIS_PANEL` |\\n| Anything else | `UNDETERMINED` (no negative/equivalence claim) |\\n\\n## 7. Preregistration checklist (what must be frozen before the first model call)\\n\\n1. This protocol (hash) + arm definitions.\\n2. Frozen item list + splits (origin-disjoint, opaque ids) + near-duplicate check receipt.\\n3. Actor freeze receipt (revision + settings + tool hash).\\n4. Checker/adapter versions + fixture PASS receipt.\\n5. Feedback-right contract (approved) + episode pool manifest (if E/C are populated).\\n6. Analysis script hash + bootstrap settings.\\n7. Budget/window binding (owner/advisor).\\n\\n## 8. Non-goals\\n\\nNo training (Memory/SFT/DPO), no production integration, no long-horizon tasks, no new domains, no method-novelty claim. Executing anything here requires the WP-1 software gate and the owner/advisor window.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"todo_list\",\"items\":[{\"text\":\"Verify contracts and input schemas\",\"completed\":false},{\"text\":\"Write and hash implementation contract\",\"completed\":false},{\"text\":\"Implement checker, adapter, fixtures\",\"completed\":false},{\"text\":\"Run synthetic obligations and preflight\",\"completed\":false},{\"text\":\"Write receipts and prereg skeleton\",\"completed\":false}]}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"set -euo pipefail\\nprintf '%s\\\\\\\\n' '--- graph-loop-rules ---'\\ncat /home/testuser/.codex/skills/graph-loop-rules/SKILL.md\\nprintf '%s\\\\\\\\n' '--- checker contract ---'\\ncat docs/research/WP0_TATQA_ADAPTER_CHECKER_CONTRACT_v1.md\\nprintf '%s\\\\\\\\n' '--- execution package ---'\\ncat docs/research/WP0_TATQA_LOOP_A_EXECUTION_PACKAGE_v1.md\\nprintf '%s\\\\\\\\n' '--- card ---'\\ncat research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/loop_a_prompt.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"set -euo pipefail\\nprintf '%s\\\\\\\\n' '--- graph-loop-rules ---'\\ncat /home/testuser/.codex/skills/graph-loop-rules/SKILL.md\\nprintf '%s\\\\\\\\n' '--- checker contract ---'\\ncat docs/research/WP0_TATQA_ADAPTER_CHECKER_CONTRACT_v1.md\\nprintf '%s\\\\\\\\n' '--- execution package ---'\\ncat docs/research/WP0_TATQA_LOOP_A_EXECUTION_PACKAGE_v1.md\\nprintf '%s\\\\\\\\n' '--- card ---'\\ncat research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/loop_a_prompt.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"--- graph-loop-rules ---\\n---\\nname: graph-loop-rules\\ndescription: JinRongAgents Graph Loop 红线与运行约束。OpenCode agent 在本仓库执行任何任务（解析、审计、问答、代码修改）前必须遵守；涉及冻结节点、生产后端、API key、72B 模型时触发。\\n---\\n\\n# Graph Loop 运行约束（OpenCode agent 适用）\\n\\n本仓库运行四层 Graph Loop（A 执行 / B 验证 / C 审计 / D 战略，见 docs/17）。任何 agent 任务必须遵守：\\n\\n## 红线（违反即失败）\\n1. 冻结节点不可修改：tests/test_m1_service.py、scripts/graph/frozen_hashes.txt、docs/m1_schema/（schema 基线文档）、以及 frozen_hashes.txt 所列全部路径（含仓库外运行时 schema ~/wzh/m1_samples/m1_table_schema.json，commit 钩子 + Loop B 双重 md5 校验）。注意：仓库内 config/m1_table_schema.json 不在冻结清单，可通过 schema API 写入并热加载（见 m1-gap-triage skill）。\\n2. 不改不重启 :5050 生产后端（甲方演示随时可用）；不切页面后端。\\n3. 不触碰、不打印、不创建 API key。\\n4. 不加载 72B 模型（已终判退化并删除）。\\n5. 归档文档用 git mv，禁止 rm；OpenCode/MCP 交付物三件（archive/09、archive/10、archive/2026-07-19_m2_mcp_verification.md）永不删除。\\n\\n## 运行纪律\\n- 每步任务结果追加到 logs/graph/dispatch_log.md（格式：[HH:MM] 任务 → 结果 → commit）。\\n- 无法判断的问题写 logs/graph/blocked_questions.md 后跳过，不阻塞。\\n- gap/遗留项台账唯一信源：memory/THREADS.md，其他文档只引用不复述。\\n- 现状以 memory/STATE.md 为准，不到历史文档里找现状。\\n- Loop A 执行层完整约束见 scripts/graph/loop_a_exec_constraints.md；Loop C 审计 prompt 见 scripts/graph/loop_c_audit_prompt.md。\\n- 需要联网检索或数值验证时用 python scripts/qwen_harness_tools.py（web_search / code_interpreter / web_extractor），不滥用。\\n\\n## 验证要求\\n交付前必须：远端 ./venv/bin/python -m pytest -q 全绿（基线 275 passed / 13 skipped）；证据先于断言（evidence before assertions）。\\n--- checker contract ---\\n# WP-0 TAT-QA Adapter and Checker Contracts v1\\n\\n> date: 2026-10-13 | author: Loop D (WP-0 item A5) | status: `SPECIFICATION_ONLY - NOT IMPLEMENTED`\\n> parents: [WP0_TATQA_PACKAGE_v1.md](WP0_TATQA_PACKAGE_v1.md), [task card](thesis_experience_v1_task_card.md), [blueprint](THESIS_EXECUTION_BLUEPRINT_v1.md) §2\\n> These contracts describe what Loop A must implement in WP-1. Nothing here is code, and nothing here authorises a run.\\n\\n## 1. Task adapter contract\\n\\n**Input:** one candidate item from `data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/candidate_items_v1.json`.\\n\\n**Actor-visible projection (what the model sees):**\\n- the table (all rows and columns, verbatim, no truncation per arm);\\n- the two period labels and the row label/identifier needed to name the row;\\n- the requested quantity and the requested target unit;\\n- the tool description (a deterministic calculator: `calc(expression) -> number`);\\n- the arm-specific context block (none for B; the experience block for E/C; the static rules for S).\\n\\n**Hidden from the actor, always:** `gold_delta_source_unit`, `gold_recompute_rule`, any derived target value, the item's origin id where it would leak the answer, and the whole `candidate_items` file.\\n\\n**Actor obligations:** choose the row, the two periods, the unit relation and the arithmetic parameter; call the calculator; the final answer must consume the calculator's returned value.\\n\\n**Answer format (fixed):** `{row: <label>, periods: [<late>, <early>], delta_source: <number>, delta_target: <number>, unit: <target unit>}` in a single JSON object, or the literal token `REFUSED` / `UNKNOWN`.\\n\\n**Determinism:** the adapter must produce byte-identical prompts for the same item and arm. No timestamps, no sampling, no arm-dependent table truncation.\\n\\n## 2. Checker contract\\n\\n**Gold recomputation (independent of the actor):** for the item's `row_index`, read `value(late)` and `value(early)` from the table cells with the stated parser (strip thousands separators, treat parentheses as negative), compute `delta_source = value(late) - value(early)`, then convert by the scale factor between `source_unit` and the requested target unit. The checker must never read the actor's output before the gold exists.\\n\\n**Scoring (per item, per arm, per repeat):**\\n| Outcome | Rule |\\n|---|---|\\n| `correct` | `delta_source` and `delta_target` both match gold exactly (after the declared rounding); row and periods match |\\n| `correct_other_form` | same value via a mathematically equivalent expression (e.g., early-minus-late with a negated sign) - counted as correct, and recorded separately |\\n| `wrong_unit` | `delta_source` correct but `delta_target` wrong |\\n| `wrong_period` | the periods chosen differ from the item's |\\n| `regressed` | compared to arm B on the same item, a previously correct answer becomes incorrect |\\n| `refused` | the literal `REFUSED` |\\n| `unknown` | the literal `UNKNOWN`, a timeout, or an unparseable answer |\\n\\n**Independent unit of analysis:** the origin (the raw record), not the item, not the repeat. Report per-origin paired differences `E-B`, `E-C`, `E-S`, `C-B`, with the origin-level differences listed explicitly.\\n\\n**Anti-leakage obligations the checker must enforce:** (a) the item's gold appears nowhere in the actor-visible projection; (b) no item shares an origin with any experience episode used in the same arm run; (c) the C-arm context differs from the E-arm context by at most 5% in context tokens; (d) the S-arm rules are frozen at development time and never edited per item.\\n\\n## 3. Fixture obligations (what Loop A must demonstrate without any model)\\n\\nOn synthetic fixtures only, Loop A must show:\\n1. the adapter emits the same prompt twice for the same item (byte equality);\\n2. the gold never appears in the projection (string search);\\n3. the checker's recomputation matches hand-computed values on at least 5 hand-built fixtures, including one with parentheses-negative cells and one with a thousands separator;\\n4. the scale conversion matches for thousand->unit, million->thousand, billion->million and percent->percent;\\n5. an `UNKNOWN` and a `REFUSED` answer are classified correctly;\\n6. the arm-context token delta between E and C is computed and reported.\\n\\n**Stop:** if any fixture obligation cannot be met, WP-1 stops and reports `SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED`. No model is called to \\\"try it out\\\".--- execution package ---\\n# WP-0 TAT-QA Loop A Execution Package v1 (DRAFT - NOT DISPATCHED)\\n\\n> date: 2026-10-13 | author: Loop D | status: `READY_TO_DISPATCH_AFTER_APPROVAL` | zero model calls; fixture-first; no training.\\n> parents: [adapter/checker contract](WP0_TATQA_ADAPTER_CHECKER_CONTRACT_v1.md), [evaluation protocol](WP0_TATQA_EVALUATION_PROTOCOL_v1.md), [task card](thesis_experience_v1_task_card.md) Sec.3-4, [exec constraints](../../scripts/graph/loop_a_exec_constraints.md), [launcher](../governance/loop_ac_launcher_v1.md).\\n\\n## 1. Preconditions (all required before dispatch)\\n\\n1. Advisor: G-RQ accepted (QUALIFIED_CONDITIONAL -> formal allowance for WP-1).\\n2. Owner/advisor: write-path permission for `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/` and `data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/` on GB10.\\n3. Actor freeze plan approved for the later stages (F1); WP-1 itself needs no model.\\n4. Dispatch via `scripts/graph/loop_ac_launcher.sh` (the designed channel), prompt file in-repo, receipt discipline per the launcher doc.\\n\\n## 2. Work items (all reversible; fixture-first; stdlib-only where possible)\\n\\n| # | Item | Deliverable | Acceptance |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| W1 | Checker implementation | `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/checker.py` (+ tests) | matches hand-computed values on 5 fixtures incl. parentheses-negative and thousands separator; taxonomy classes incl. `REFUSED`/`UNKNOWN` |\\n| W2 | Adapter implementation | `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/adapter.py` (+ tests) | byte-identical prompts for same item+arm; hidden-gold search clean; opaque ids; no arm-dependent truncation |\\n| W3 | Fixture suite (A5 Sec.3, six obligations) | `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/fixtures/` + receipt | all six obligations PASS, incl. E/C token-delta computation; fail-closed |\\n| W4 | Execution preflight | `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/PREFLIGHT_RECEIPT.json` | required files exist; schema fields match runtime payload; scorer defined on allowed inputs; provenance writer attributes to the task; metric pipeline runs on NON-SCIENTIFIC fixtures; no held-out reads |\\n| W5 | Freeze assembly (with Loop D) | prereg draft + hash pins | protocol/item/split/actor/checker hashes resolve |\\n\\n## 3. Non-goals / prohibitions\\n\\n- No model calls, no episode collection, no context-block construction, no training (Memory/SFT/DPO), no production services, no change to any frozen Paper E asset.\\n- No edits outside the two write paths above; receipts required for every claim; `SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED` stop on any fixture failure (do not \\\"try it out\\\" with a model).\\n\\n## 4. Stop and escalation\\n\\n- Any acceptance failure -> stop, report `SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED` with the failing fixture.\\n- After W1-W5 PASS + C pre-result audit PASS -> only then request pilot (WP-2) authorisation; budget/window must be bound first.\\n\\n## 5. Dispatch template (when approved)\\n\\n```\\nbash scripts/graph/loop_ac_launcher.sh start a tatqa-wp1-<date> research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/loop_a_prompt.md 14400\\n```\\n\\nPrompt file must state: scope = W1-W5 only; write paths; receipts; fail-closed; no model/services.\\n--- card ---\\n# Loop A Assignment - TAT-QA WP-1 (thin runner: checker + adapter + fixtures + preflight; NO MODEL CALLS)\\n\\nCARD: research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/loop_a_prompt.md | dispatched 2026-10-13 by Loop D under owner approval.\\nROLE: Loop A / GB10 implementation. You implement ONE bounded software package (WP-1) plus its non-scientific fixture checks. Nothing else. Model calls = 0. This card authorises NO pilot run and NO episode collection.\\n\\nCONTRACT (read first; binding):\\n- docs/research/WP0_TATQA_ADAPTER_CHECKER_CONTRACT_v1.md  (THE specification for checker/adapter/fixtures)\\n- docs/research/WP0_TATQA_LOOP_A_EXECUTION_PACKAGE_v1.md  (W1-W5 + acceptance criteria)\\n- docs/research/WP0_TATQA_EVALUATION_PROTOCOL_v1.md  (context only; do not execute anything)\\n- data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/origin_manifest.json, candidate_items_v1.json, GENERATION_RECEIPT.json  (READ-ONLY)\\n- data/research/tatqa_raw_2026/tatqa_dataset_train.json, tatqa_dataset_dev.json  (READ-ONLY)\\n\\nProject dir (your cwd): /home/testuser/wzh/projects/agents_final_tech\\nWork dir (create; NEW): research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/\\nData out (create; NEW): data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/\\n\\nPINNED INPUTS (verify BEFORE anything else; mismatch -> STOP, report HASH_MISMATCH):\\n- candidate_items_v1.json sha256 bc55fe7a53381f32e5d84ff6c17ced18ec72fd322f98a9f80c4eccb714caac12\\n- origin_manifest.json sha256 3718e6fef4d52bec0c1c29b47ba9ab60e298754b9e8527835d09c9d223d70cea\\n- tatqa_dataset_train.json sha256 2df6e722cdbaaa37efcbfb280f5c9a15be29a6ec18f618ef936fe63cc6d07c69\\n- tatqa_dataset_dev.json sha256 8da095a819af6db3c14877c6df2d4d29960e41d1a63dd1fa853507bd2a616af5\\n- expected counts: 60 candidate items; 182 origins.\\n\\nPRE-RUN (mandatory order):\\n1) Verify the four hashes (sha256sum) and the two counts from GENERATION_RECEIPT.json.\\n2) Write research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/implementation_contract.md first: module list, function signatures, fixture plan, receipt schema, exact commands you will run; hash the contract before running anything.\\n3) Implement W1-W5, then run ONLY the synthetic fixture suite.\\n\\nWORK ITEMS (spec = adapter/checker contract; acceptance = execution package Sec.2):\\nW1 checker.py - gold recomputed from table cells (strip thousands separators; parentheses = negative), scale conversion (thousand->unit, million->thousand, billion->million, percent->percent), outcome taxonomy including correct_other_form / REFUSED / UNKNOWN; gold exists before any answer is read.\\nW2 adapter.py - deterministic actor-visible projection (verbatim, no truncation), fixed answer format, hidden fields (gold etc.) never leaked, opaque item/origin ids, byte-identical prompt for the same item+arm; arm context hooks for B/E/C/S as typed placeholders only (real experience blocks are NOT built here).\\nW3 fixtures/ + run_fixtures.py - the six obligations: (1) byte-equal prompts; (2) hidden-gold string search clean; (3) >=5 hand-built recompute fixtures incl. one parentheses-negative and one thousands-separator case; (4) the four scale conversions; (5) UNKNOWN + REFUSED classification; (6) E/C context token-delta accounting. SYNTHETIC fixtures only; never read held-out outcomes.\\nW4 PREFLIGHT_RECEIPT.json - required files exist; schema field names match the runtime payload; checker defined on all allowed inputs; group/split ids resolve; provenance writer attributes to this task; the metric pipeline runs end-to-end on NON-SCIENTIFIC fixtures; no held-out result read.\\nW5 PREREG_DRAFT_SKELETON.md + hash pins (checker/adapter/fixtures/preflight hashes); actor fields marked PENDING (advisor selection; do NOT touch model files or weights).\\n\\nSTYLE: python3 stdlib only; LF outputs; tests runnable via `python3 research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/run_fixtures.py`; no pytest dependency.\\n\\nFORBIDDEN: model/judge calls; network; services/databases; training; commit/push; editing paper/, docs/, pinned inputs, or anything outside the two write dirs; scoring candidate items (READ allowed, SCORE not allowed; fixtures are synthetic); running loop_b_verify.sh; fabricating or weakening any test.\\nSTOP CONDITIONS: hash mismatch -> HASH_MISMATCH; any fixture obligation fails -> STOP and report SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED naming the failing item (never adjust the test to pass); a forbidden action being required -> stop and report.\\n\\nOUTPUTS: the files above + research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/WP1_RECEIPT.json (valid JSON, no fences): task, start/end UTC, re-verified input hashes, artifact hashes (checker/adapter/fixtures/preflight/contract), per-obligation fixture results, preflight results, cost (model_calls=0, endpoint_calls=0), unverified items, deviations (expect none).\\n\\nEND: final message = status + receipt path + one-line summary.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat docs/research/WP0_TATQA_ADAPTER_CHECKER_CONTRACT_v1.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat docs/research/WP0_TATQA_ADAPTER_CHECKER_CONTRACT_v1.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# WP-0 TAT-QA Adapter and Checker Contracts v1\\n\\n> date: 2026-10-13 | author: Loop D (WP-0 item A5) | status: `SPECIFICATION_ONLY - NOT IMPLEMENTED`\\n> parents: [WP0_TATQA_PACKAGE_v1.md](WP0_TATQA_PACKAGE_v1.md), [task card](thesis_experience_v1_task_card.md), [blueprint](THESIS_EXECUTION_BLUEPRINT_v1.md) §2\\n> These contracts describe what Loop A must implement in WP-1. Nothing here is code, and nothing here authorises a run.\\n\\n## 1. Task adapter contract\\n\\n**Input:** one candidate item from `data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/candidate_items_v1.json`.\\n\\n**Actor-visible projection (what the model sees):**\\n- the table (all rows and columns, verbatim, no truncation per arm);\\n- the two period labels and the row label/identifier needed to name the row;\\n- the requested quantity and the requested target unit;\\n- the tool description (a deterministic calculator: `calc(expression) -> number`);\\n- the arm-specific context block (none for B; the experience block for E/C; the static rules for S).\\n\\n**Hidden from the actor, always:** `gold_delta_source_unit`, `gold_recompute_rule`, any derived target value, the item's origin id where it would leak the answer, and the whole `candidate_items` file.\\n\\n**Actor obligations:** choose the row, the two periods, the unit relation and the arithmetic parameter; call the calculator; the final answer must consume the calculator's returned value.\\n\\n**Answer format (fixed):** `{row: <label>, periods: [<late>, <early>], delta_source: <number>, delta_target: <number>, unit: <target unit>}` in a single JSON object, or the literal token `REFUSED` / `UNKNOWN`.\\n\\n**Determinism:** the adapter must produce byte-identical prompts for the same item and arm. No timestamps, no sampling, no arm-dependent table truncation.\\n\\n## 2. Checker contract\\n\\n**Gold recomputation (independent of the actor):** for the item's `row_index`, read `value(late)` and `value(early)` from the table cells with the stated parser (strip thousands separators, treat parentheses as negative), compute `delta_source = value(late) - value(early)`, then convert by the scale factor between `source_unit` and the requested target unit. The checker must never read the actor's output before the gold exists.\\n\\n**Scoring (per item, per arm, per repeat):**\\n| Outcome | Rule |\\n|---|---|\\n| `correct` | `delta_source` and `delta_target` both match gold exactly (after the declared rounding); row and periods match |\\n| `correct_other_form` | same value via a mathematically equivalent expression (e.g., early-minus-late with a negated sign) - counted as correct, and recorded separately |\\n| `wrong_unit` | `delta_source` correct but `delta_target` wrong |\\n| `wrong_period` | the periods chosen differ from the item's |\\n| `regressed` | compared to arm B on the same item, a previously correct answer becomes incorrect |\\n| `refused` | the literal `REFUSED` |\\n| `unknown` | the literal `UNKNOWN`, a timeout, or an unparseable answer |\\n\\n**Independent unit of analysis:** the origin (the raw record), not the item, not the repeat. Report per-origin paired differences `E-B`, `E-C`, `E-S`, `C-B`, with the origin-level differences listed explicitly.\\n\\n**Anti-leakage obligations the checker must enforce:** (a) the item's gold appears nowhere in the actor-visible projection; (b) no item shares an origin with any experience episode used in the same arm run; (c) the C-arm context differs from the E-arm context by at most 5% in context tokens; (d) the S-arm rules are frozen at development time and never edited per item.\\n\\n## 3. Fixture obligations (what Loop A must demonstrate without any model)\\n\\nOn synthetic fixtures only, Loop A must show:\\n1. the adapter emits the same prompt twice for the same item (byte equality);\\n2. the gold never appears in the projection (string search);\\n3. the checker's recomputation matches hand-computed values on at least 5 hand-built fixtures, including one with parentheses-negative cells and one with a thousands separator;\\n4. the scale conversion matches for thousand->unit, million->thousand, billion->million and percent->percent;\\n5. an `UNKNOWN` and a `REFUSED` answer are classified correctly;\\n6. the arm-context token delta between E and C is computed and reported.\\n\\n**Stop:** if any fixture obligation cannot be met, WP-1 stops and reports `SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED`. No model is called to \\\"try it out\\\".\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat docs/research/WP0_TATQA_LOOP_A_EXECUTION_PACKAGE_v1.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat docs/research/WP0_TATQA_LOOP_A_EXECUTION_PACKAGE_v1.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# WP-0 TAT-QA Loop A Execution Package v1 (DRAFT - NOT DISPATCHED)\\n\\n> date: 2026-10-13 | author: Loop D | status: `READY_TO_DISPATCH_AFTER_APPROVAL` | zero model calls; fixture-first; no training.\\n> parents: [adapter/checker contract](WP0_TATQA_ADAPTER_CHECKER_CONTRACT_v1.md), [evaluation protocol](WP0_TATQA_EVALUATION_PROTOCOL_v1.md), [task card](thesis_experience_v1_task_card.md) Sec.3-4, [exec constraints](../../scripts/graph/loop_a_exec_constraints.md), [launcher](../governance/loop_ac_launcher_v1.md).\\n\\n## 1. Preconditions (all required before dispatch)\\n\\n1. Advisor: G-RQ accepted (QUALIFIED_CONDITIONAL -> formal allowance for WP-1).\\n2. Owner/advisor: write-path permission for `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/` and `data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/` on GB10.\\n3. Actor freeze plan approved for the later stages (F1); WP-1 itself needs no model.\\n4. Dispatch via `scripts/graph/loop_ac_launcher.sh` (the designed channel), prompt file in-repo, receipt discipline per the launcher doc.\\n\\n## 2. Work items (all reversible; fixture-first; stdlib-only where possible)\\n\\n| # | Item | Deliverable | Acceptance |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| W1 | Checker implementation | `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/checker.py` (+ tests) | matches hand-computed values on 5 fixtures incl. parentheses-negative and thousands separator; taxonomy classes incl. `REFUSED`/`UNKNOWN` |\\n| W2 | Adapter implementation | `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/adapter.py` (+ tests) | byte-identical prompts for same item+arm; hidden-gold search clean; opaque ids; no arm-dependent truncation |\\n| W3 | Fixture suite (A5 Sec.3, six obligations) | `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/fixtures/` + receipt | all six obligations PASS, incl. E/C token-delta computation; fail-closed |\\n| W4 | Execution preflight | `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/PREFLIGHT_RECEIPT.json` | required files exist; schema fields match runtime payload; scorer defined on allowed inputs; provenance writer attributes to the task; metric pipeline runs on NON-SCIENTIFIC fixtures; no held-out reads |\\n| W5 | Freeze assembly (with Loop D) | prereg draft + hash pins | protocol/item/split/actor/checker hashes resolve |\\n\\n## 3. Non-goals / prohibitions\\n\\n- No model calls, no episode collection, no context-block construction, no training (Memory/SFT/DPO), no production services, no change to any frozen Paper E asset.\\n- No edits outside the two write paths above; receipts required for every claim; `SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED` stop on any fixture failure (do not \\\"try it out\\\" with a model).\\n\\n## 4. Stop and escalation\\n\\n- Any acceptance failure -> stop, report `SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED` with the failing fixture.\\n- After W1-W5 PASS + C pre-result audit PASS -> only then request pilot (WP-2) authorisation; budget/window must be bound first.\\n\\n## 5. Dispatch template (when approved)\\n\\n```\\nbash scripts/graph/loop_ac_launcher.sh start a tatqa-wp1-<date> research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/loop_a_prompt.md 14400\\n```\\n\\nPrompt file must state: scope = W1-W5 only; write paths; receipts; fail-closed; no model/services.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nimport json\\n